// Type checking for the test files, which the main configuration does not look
// at.
//
// tsconfig.json excludes __tests__ so that a build writes only src/ into dist/.
// The side effect was that neither `npm run typecheck` nor CI ever type checked
// a test file: a required field added to a shared type made every stand-in in
// the tests invalid while tsc kept reporting success, and it surfaced at runtime
// when vitest tripped over undefined. That is the lucky version. A wrong cast on
// a path no test walks would not surface at all.
//
// Three things have to be overridden rather than inherited, and the first is the
// one that looks fine and checks nothing:
//
//   - `exclude`, or the inherited list keeps __tests__ out and this file
//     type checks zero files while reporting success. Measured while writing it.
//   - `rootDir`, which is "src" upstream. Left in place it produces one TS6059
//     per test file ("not under rootDir"), even with noEmit, burying the real
//     errors in noise.
//   - `noEmit`, because this configuration exists to check, not to build. It
//     also makes the inherited outDir and declaration harmless.
//
// Everything else is inherited on purpose. Test files are held to the same
// strictness as src/, including exactOptionalPropertyTypes and
// noUncheckedIndexedAccess, because a stand-in built loosely is a stand-in that
// stops resembling the thing it stands in for.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "rootDir": ".",
    "noEmit": true
  },
  "include": ["__tests__/**/*", "src/**/*"],
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "dist"]
}
